<p>President Trump sharply criticized NATO this week after several European allies declined to back the United States in the Iran war by authorizing use of military bases or airspace. The dispute surfaced during and around a White House meeting with NATO Secretary General Mark Rutte. France and Spain reportedly refused to grant the US access to military facilities for operations related to Iran, deepening long-running arguments inside the alliance over burden-sharing, strategic priorities, and the terms of US support for European security. In the latest development, Trump has discussed with advisers the option of pulling some US troops from Europe, according to a senior White House official cited by Reuters through The Straits Times. His frustration also reflects allied reluctance to help secure the Strait of Hormuz. European officials and Rutte have tried to steady the alliance rather than inflame the clash, even as the strain remains public.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/YdVzf_lkzRtLsGE0aQago3OVQrnmS-KKN5qObEmta3A3zIa2Ro6KF0qAYoCTMBuxW0t24vCRQsn6WgLNMlkuAsQh_bN0Ebi3jpNFxkVX7XX3He0jEWJyru8ME0X2-4JVJ27SkBA0QtIvUrEgHhEAszY44D8Fuk5HK6fwxsmCz6HquOvgFyIfAA2PkWreCozkEx1cmoKE_9g' alt='President Trump and Mark Rutte, the secretary general of NATO, in the Netherlands in June. The two met again in Washington this week, as the war in Iran has deepened the gulf between Mr. Trump and the alliance.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>White House specifics: Politico reported that Trump&#x27;s hourslong private meeting with Rutte focused on allied refusals over bases and airspace. He made no specific demand and did not explicitly tie the issue to a cut in US alliance commitments.</li><li>Limited ask: Secretary of State Marco Rubio said allies were not being asked to conduct airstrikes themselves, making clear that the immediate US request was for access, not direct European combat participation.</li><li>Alliance anxiety: Euronews reported that Trump&#x27;s criticism quickly revived fears that he could try to pull the United States out of the nearly 80-year-old alliance.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Trump: Politico reported that Trump viewed the refusals as a betrayal by allies who, in his view, benefit from military infrastructure and security support built on American largesse. The episode reinforced his longstanding complaint that Europeans are freeloaders. (<a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/04/09/trump-rutte-meeting-iran-nato-00866031'>Politico</a>)</li><li>White House official: Reuters, via The Straits Times, reported that Trump&#x27;s frustration with NATO allies was also tied to the lack of progress on his plans to acquire Greenland, broadening the dispute beyond the immediate Iran-war basing fight. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/trump-weighs-pulling-some-us-troops-from-europe-amid-nato-strains-official-says'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Le Monde analysis: Le Monde argued that Trump&#x27;s criticism of NATO has weakened the Atlantic alliance and may be aimed at shifting blame for US setbacks in the Gulf to Europe. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/opinion/article/2026/04/09/trump-s-anti-nato-outbursts-have-undeniably-weakened-the-atlantic-pact_6752268_23.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/09/us/politics/trump-iran-nato-rutte.html'>Amid Trump’s Threats, NATO Labors to Survive the Iran War</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/e2347e81-19b2-4cd5-aea4-ff6bacf0e71b'>Nato split over US access to European bases in Iran war</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/trump-weighs-pulling-some-us-troops-from-europe-amid-nato-strains-official-says'>Trump weighs pulling some US troops from Europe amid NATO strains, official says</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/opinion/article/2026/04/09/trump-s-anti-nato-outbursts-have-undeniably-weakened-the-atlantic-pact_6752268_23.html'>&#x27;Trump&#x27;s anti-NATO outbursts have undeniably weakened the Atlantic pact&#x27;</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/04/09/trump-again-berates-nato-calls-it-disappointing'>Trump again berates NATO, calls it &#x27;disappointing&#x27;</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/04/09/trump-rutte-meeting-iran-nato-00866031'>What Trump’s blowup with Rutte was really about</a> - politico.com</li></ul>